### Pin the runner image version

Runs executed on Scalr-managed agent pools use the account default runner image unless the workspace is pinned to a specific image version.
The `runner_image_version_id` attribute can only be used with Scalr-managed agent pools: it cannot be combined with an `agent_pool_id` that points to a self-hosted agent pool.
When `agent_pool_id` is not set, the environment or account default agent pool must be Scalr-managed.
Looking up or pinning an image version requires the `container-images:read` permission on the account.
Without it, the data sources fail with a permission error, and a pinned version ID fails with a "not found or user unauthorized" error.

Remove the attribute to fall back to the account default.
If a workspace is pinned in the Scalr UI and its configuration does not set `runner_image_version_id`, the next apply removes the pin.

{{tffile "examples/resources/scalr_workspace/runner_image.tf" }}

To follow the latest version, omit `version` in `scalr_container_image_version`.
Terraform reads the data source on every plan, so the workspace moves to a newer version on the next apply after Scalr syncs it. Until then, runs use the pinned version.
Scalr syncs image tags once a day, so a newly pushed tag can take up to a day to appear.
If the latest tag is removed from the registry, the next apply moves the workspace to the new latest version, which is usually older.
Do not use `latest_version_id` of `scalr_container_image` for this: it is null when the image has no versions, and the workspace is then silently unpinned.

